-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-# Layerwise GPU prefill (recipe E22 / T3.6b2).
-#
-# The CPU tier is ~50x slower than the GPUs on a prefill chunk (216 tok/s vs
-# ~8K tok/s all-GPU), so for chunks of at least KT_GPU_PREFILL_MIN_TOKENS
-# tokens the CPU experts are *streamed* to the GPUs instead of computed on the
-# CPU: kt-kernel exports each CPU expert's packed MXFP4 bytes and bf16 scales
-# (write_weight_scale_to_buffer, one TP slice per rank) into a pinned host
-# buffer shared by both TP ranks, each rank DMAs its slice into a per-rank
-# staging set of expert slots laid out for the FlashInfer SM120 CUTLASS MoE,
-# and the layer runs the fused kernel twice: once over the resident GPU
-# experts and once over the staged CPU experts. The export of layer L+1 is
-# submitted while layer L computes (host double buffer), so per layer the
-# cost is ~max(export, H2D + GEMM). Measured on this host (E22a): export
-# 68 ms/layer at 52 GB/s (core-bound, scales with KT_CPUINFER), H2D 37 ms
-# to both cards, pipelined ~87 ms/layer; vs ~19 s/layer-chunk on the CPU path
-# at 4096 tokens.
-#
-# Decode and short chunks keep the CPU path untouched. Ranks coordinate via
-# the TP group's gloo cpu_group: one barrier when the host buffer is filled
-# and one before it is overwritten. 0 (default) disables the feature.
-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
